{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/545284-cost-of-wolf-gifts-is-the-text-or-the-table-correct","id":545284,"title":"Cost of Wolf Gifts - Is the text or the table correct?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-08T08:26:47-07:00","id":545284,"title":"Cost of Wolf Gifts - Is the text or the table correct?","content":"The table on page 84 says Wolf Gift Facets cost one Experience, but the text on page 85 says they costs two experiences.<br /> <br /> Which is correct? One Experience does sound really, really cheap...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:36:17-07:00","id":545339,"title":"","content":"As per the text in the Gifts rules themselves, Wolf Facets cost 1 Experience each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:37:40-07:00","id":545342,"title":"","content":"Whichever says 1 Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:31:08-07:00","id":545507,"title":"","content":"1 Experience is the same cost as a skill specialty or a 1-dot Ritual or Merit, all of which can be very useful, but are not typically earthshatteringly powerful.<br /> <br /> That's true of Wolf Gifts as well. Knowing where your pack-mates are within a few miles is generally about as handy as consistently knowing which direction is which. <br /> Being able to take Gauru for Rites might give you an extra die or two if they're very physical Rites, but it opens you the risk of more fleshly breaking points, which are dangerous for a young character. <br /> Being able to track by impossible means gives you a couple extra dice if you're way behind you're target, a situation where you have more to worry about than lost dice. It also brings your character more in line with the general Werewolf concept of &quot;Consumate Hunter&quot;.<br /> Being able to use your Gifts when you're not there is cool, too, but your Gifts then become significantly more expensive to use and you can't automatically see what you're doing.<br /> <br /> In all, their power level is either low-ish or mitigated somewhat by an intrinsic risk or added cost.<br /> I'm a huge fan of the Wolf Gifts and took most of the Wisdom ones for my Ithaeur as quickly as I could. I don't think it's ridiculous that they're that cheap, thouh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://for